Subject: Cantor Instance Foundation P0 Solution

@ [solution_uuid] 9488dbad-865e-4c56-9b7b-f40c2fe5a887
@ [specification_uuid] d7e6055f-d40e-46c4-a757-2db3b77c7108

& [Solution]
  + a provider-free cantor_instance_contract crate owns strict instance and kernel capability forms
  + deterministic validation and compatibility compilation produce only admitted or held structural results
  + role constraints prevent an Eclipse UI adapter package or evidence artifact from masquerading as the Cantor kernel
  + a read-only semantic custody builder hashes the selected live candidate surface and records excluded generated roots
  + an independent verifier replays inventory path policy identity size and SHA256 from the live source checkpoint

& [InitialInstanceBoundary]
  + Cantor kernel: semantic graph custody compiled guards attention lifecycle audit provider interfaces and update governance
  + SOP Eclipse adapter: workbench views recipe builder project navigation presentation and user workflow
  + instance packages: governed SOP recipes subjects perspectives and domain content
  + generated payload: evidence reports distributions copied operators workspaces archives and temporary build state

& [FuturePromotion]
  + each selected live component receives its own source custody compatibility review tests and implementation evidence on the current Cantor line
  + the existing untracked cantor_scribe Rust crate is a high-value candidate but is not accepted wholesale by this P0 formation

& [VerifiedBoundary]
  + the Eclipse adapter and package fixture is structurally admitted while the same fixture with cantor_scribe in a kernel slot is deterministically held for separate promotion
  + the retained custody and compatibility evidence is replayable under PowerShell 7 and Windows PowerShell 5.1 and grants no execution provider installation update publication or effect authority
